            <div id='newReviews'>
              <div class="section"><h4>New Movies in Theaters & Coming Soon</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/movie-reviews/tron-legacy"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/tron_legacy_ver2.jpg" alt="tron_legacy_ver2.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1167661" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>TRON: Legacy</span> (2010, Rated PG)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this is one of the most buzzed-about movies of 2010 and will especially appeal to kids and teens who are into sci-fi. With many fans on alert since Disney unveiled the eye-popping trailer, this sequel to the 1982 cult classic Tron ... <a href="/movie-reviews/tron-legacy#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>2+</span></div><h5><a href="/movie-reviews/tron-legacy">TRON: Legacy</a></h5><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">1</span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/movie-reviews/yogi-bear"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/yogi_bear.jpg" alt="yogi_bear.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1167662" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Yogi Bear</span> (2010, Rated PG)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that Yogi Bear returns -- this time on the big screen -- in this half-animated, half-live-action 3-D family comedy. Yogi &quot;Smarter Than Your Average Bear&quot; (voiced by Dan Aykroyd) and sidekick Boo-Boo (Justin Timberlake) wander ... <a href="/movie-reviews/yogi-bear#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>2+</span></div><h5><a href="/movie-reviews/yogi-bear">Yogi Bear</a></h5><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">1</span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div style="visibility:hidden;"  class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/movie-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/chronicles_of_narnia_the_voyage_of_the_dawn_treader.jpg" alt="chronicles_of_narnia_the_voyage_of_the_dawn_treader.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1167666" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader</span> (2010, Rated PG)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that the third Chronicles of Narnia installment is, like its predecessors, a tween-friendly fantasy adventure. In general, you can expect the same level of special effects-heightened battles/violence and minor language as Prince Caspian. ... <a href="/movie-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>10+</span></div><h5><a href="/movie-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader">The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/movie-reviews">movie reviews</a></div></div><div class="section"><h4>New Video Game Reviews</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/game-reviews/tron-evolution"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Tron_Evolution_Box.jpg" alt="Tron_Evolution_Box.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1188985" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>TRON: Evolution</span> (PlayStation 3, Windows, Xbox 360)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> TRON: Evolution is a game based on the movie TRON: Legacy. It earned its &quot;Teen&quot; rating primarily for its fantasy violence.This includes hand-to-hand combat, acrobatic attacks, throwing discs, shooting tanks, and racing in light ... <a href="/game-reviews/tron-evolution#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>13+</span></div><h5><a href="/game-reviews/tron-evolution">TRON: Evolution</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/game-reviews/michael-jackson-experience"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/MJ_Box.jpg" alt="MJ_Box.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1187235" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Michael Jackson: The Experience</span> (Nintendo DS, Nintendo Wii, PSP)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> Michael Jackson The Experience is rated &quot;E10+&quot; for some suggestive lyrics (mainly sexual, a little violent) and there are some suggestive moves, too, including thrusting hips and crotch-grabbing. But at its core, this is a ... <a href="/game-reviews/michael-jackson-experience#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>10+</span></div><h5><a href="/game-reviews/michael-jackson-experience">Michael Jackson: The Experience</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/game-reviews/disney-tangled"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Disney_Tangled.jpg" alt="Disney_Tangled.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1185537" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Disney Tangled</span> (Nintendo DS, Nintendo DSi, Nintendo Wii)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that Disney Tangled is based on the film of the same name and that many children will likely want to play it simply because of its recognizable title and characters. It features some mild cartoon violence of the whack-a-bad-guy variety; ... <a href="/game-reviews/disney-tangled#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>8+</span></div><h5><a href="/game-reviews/disney-tangled">Disney Tangled</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">2</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/game-reviews">game reviews</a></div></div><div class="section"><h4>Popular Websites for Kids</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/website-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Narnia.jpg" alt="Narnia.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1189189" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading">The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader</span> <div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that you must be 13 to register; registration is required to earn points to customize your ship. The site also features frequent pushes to Facebook. <a href="/website-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>13+</span></div><h5><a href="/website-reviews/chronicles-narnia-voyage-dawn-treader">The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/website-reviews/northpole"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/northpole_PI2.jpg" alt="northpole_PI2.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1166654" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading">Northpole</span> <div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this Christmas-themed site has made an effort to make sure kids have a safe experience. Kids can chat with digital elves, but they only receive pre-determined responses (kids can enter bad words, but they don't appear on screen and ... <a href="/website-reviews/northpole#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>7+</span></div><h5><a href="/website-reviews/northpole">Northpole</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/website-reviews/elfyourself"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Elf.jpg" alt="Elf.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1187434" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading">ElfYourself</span> <div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that on ElfYourself users can upload an image and create a dancing elf video without registering or entering any personal information. You can also email the video to acquaintances by just entering your email address and the recipient's ... <a href="/website-reviews/elfyourself#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>14+</span></div><h5><a href="/website-reviews/elfyourself">ElfYourself</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/website-reviews">website reviews</a></div></div><div class="section"><h4>TV for Kids</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/tv-reviews/christmas-cupid"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/121484_D_0039_pre.jpg" alt="121484_D_0039_pre.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1188778" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Christmas Cupid</span> (ABC Family)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this movie is not for tweens thanks to a fair amount of cursing (“damn,” “hell,” “ass,” and the like), sexual implications (mostly in dialogue, plus a few passionate kisses), and some heavy drinking from a main character, ... <a href="/tv-reviews/christmas-cupid#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>14+</span></div><h5><a href="/tv-reviews/christmas-cupid">Christmas Cupid</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/tv-reviews/gruffalo"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Gruffalo_TV.jpg" alt="Gruffalo_TV.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1188719" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>The Gruffalo</span> (ABC Family)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this beautiful adaptation is based on the acclaimed children’s book of the same name, so youngsters might be encouraged to follow up watching it with a reading session. A few scenes show Mouse envisioning being eaten by the ... <a href="/tv-reviews/gruffalo#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>3+</span></div><h5><a href="/tv-reviews/gruffalo">The Gruffalo</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/tv-reviews/vice-guide-everything"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/viceguide.jpg" alt="viceguide.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1188944" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>The Vice Guide To Everything</span> (MTV, MTV2)</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this edgy series features Vice Magazine team members as they report on political, cultural, and other stories from around the world that may not be covered in mainstream media. Stories may contain sexual content (like stripping), ... <a href="/tv-reviews/vice-guide-everything#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_yellow">Age <span>15+</span></div><h5><a href="/tv-reviews/vice-guide-everything">The Vice Guide To Everything</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/tv-reviews">TV reviews</a></div></div><div class="section"><h4>New Books for Kids</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/book-reviews/mockingbird"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/mockingbird.jpg" alt="mockingbird.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1184717" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Mockingbird</span> by Kathryn Erskine</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this winner of the 2010 National Book Award for Young People's Literature is insightful, and imparts a hopeful message. Part of the story is about how the community copes with a shooting at Virginia Dare Middle School that took the ... <a href="/book-reviews/mockingbird#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>10+</span></div><h5><a href="/book-reviews/mockingbird">Mockingbird</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">5</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="on"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/book-reviews/diary-wimpy-kid-ugly-truth"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/the_ugly_truth_book.jpg" alt="the_ugly_truth_book.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1182950" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Diary of a Wimpy Kid: The Ugly Truth</span> by Jeff Kinney</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this fifth book in the incredibly popular Wimpy Kid series features the same clueless, often irresponsible Wimpy Kid, but now he's about to go through puberty. Expect a few more references to the Big Change, but no real details ... <a href="/book-reviews/diary-wimpy-kid-ugly-truth#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>9+</span></div><h5><a href="/book-reviews/diary-wimpy-kid-ugly-truth">Diary of a Wimpy Kid: The Ugly Truth</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/book-reviews/thee-i-sing"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/of_thee_I_sing_book.jpg" alt="of_thee_I_sing_book.jpg" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1189077" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Of Thee I Sing</span> by Barack Obama</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this inspirational picture book written by President Barack Obama for his daughters focuses on the lives of 13 American heroes. The list is quite diverse -- both in terms of what these heroes look like and the work that they did. ... <a href="/book-reviews/thee-i-sing#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>4+</span></div><h5><a href="/book-reviews/thee-i-sing">Of Thee I Sing</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/book-reviews">book reviews</a></div></div><div class="section"><h4>Music to Download</h4><div class="container"><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/music-reviews/beginning"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/bep_beg.JPG" alt="bep_beg.JPG" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1186947" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>The Beginning</span> by The Black Eyed Peas</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this album is relatively mild in terms of adult content compared to other pop/hip-hop tunes and past Black Eyed Peas records. Many of the songs talk about &quot;partying&quot; but focus more on simply dancing than drinking or sex. ... <a href="/music-reviews/beginning#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>13+</span></div><h5><a href="/music-reviews/beginning">The Beginning</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/music-reviews/glee-music-christmas-album"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/glee_xmas.JPG" alt="glee_xmas.JPG" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1183969" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>Glee: The Music, The Christmas Album</span> by Glee Cast</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this CD is one of Glee's most appropriate musical releases for younger audiences. While the cast still slips in an eyebrow-raising line here and there, the majority of these songs are Christmas classics with very clean lyrics. The ... <a href="/music-reviews/glee-music-christmas-album#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>10+</span></div><h5><a href="/music-reviews/glee-music-christmas-album">Glee: The Music, The Christmas Album</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">3</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="off"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div><div class="teaser last"><div class="hpImage"><a href="/music-reviews/theres-place-us"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/homepage_teaser_image/Carrie-Underwood.png" alt="Carrie-Underwood.png" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-homepage_teaser_image" /></a></div><div id="rollover-nid-1184275" class="rollover"><div class="rollover-inner"><span class="heading"><span>"There's a Place for Us"</span> by Carrie Underwood</span><div class="summary"><h5>Parents Need to Know...</h5><p> that this single is the theme song to Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader. Sung by Carrie Underwood, it's a power ballad with a great message about never giving up and staying true to who you are; unlike the Narnia ... <a href="/music-reviews/theres-place-us#what-parents-need-to-know">read more</a></p></div><div class="rollover-user-actions" style="margin-top:-20px">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="recommended_age age_green">Age <span>6+</span></div><h5><a href="/music-reviews/theres-place-us">&quot;There&#039;s a Place for Us&quot;</a></h5><div class="fivestar-widget-static fivestar-widget-static-vote fivestar-widget-static-5 clear-block"><div class="star star-1 star-odd star-first"><span class="on">4</span></div><div class="star star-2 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-3 star-odd"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-4 star-even"><span class="on"></span></div><div class="star star-5 star-odd star-last"><span class="off"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="moreLink">More <a href="/music-reviews">music reviews</a></div></div>            </div> <!-- end newReviews -->
            <div id='advice'>
              <h4>Advice for Parents &amp; Educators</h4><p class="promo"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/web_review_profile/images/harry.jpg" alt="" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-web_review_profile" /> Check out what's new in theaters for your family.<a href="http://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews"> New kids' movies now playing</a></p><p class="promo"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/web_review_profile/images/scary_movie.jpg" alt="" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-web_review_profile" /> Can 3-D Movies Be Harmful?<a href="http://www.commonsensemedia.org/3-d-okay-your-kids"> Don't go lightly into that 3-D movie. What you need to know about 3-D.</a></p><p class="promo"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/default/files/imagecache/web_review_profile/images/Icon-GirlOnLaptop.jpg" alt="" title=""  class="imagecache imagecache-web_review_profile" />Online Games Guide Advice, tips, and great <a href="/online-games" style="display:inline">online games</a> for every age</p><h4>Want More Great Advice?</h4><p>What can you do to help your kids? <a href="/advice-for-parents">Find great tips on everything from avoiding violent tv to online safety.</a></p><h4>Are You an Educator?</h4><p>Join our educators&lsquo; program <a href="/educators"><img src="http://cdn1.www.commonsensemedia.org/sites/www.commonsensemedia.org/themes/csm_drupal/images/buttons/Joinbutton.gif" alt="Join" title="Join" width="45" height="23" /></a></p><h4>Top Family &amp; Kids Lists</h4><div class="item-list"><ul id="recLists"><li class="odd first"><a href="/game-lists/gift-ideas-our-kids-games-picks">Gift Ideas: Our Kids&#039; Games Picks</a></li><li class="even"><a href="/book-lists/gift-ideas-our-kids-book-picks">Gift Ideas: Our Kids&#039; Book Picks</a></li><li class="odd"><a href="/music-lists/gift-ideas-music">Gift Ideas: Our Kids&#039; Music Picks</a></li><li class="even"><a href="/movie-lists/gift-ideas-movies">Gift Ideas: Our Kids&#039; Movie Picks</a></li><li class="odd last"><a href="/mobile-app-lists/gift-ideas-apps">Gift Ideas: Our Kids&#039; App Picks</a></li></ul></div><p><a href="/movie-lists">See more lists</a></p>            </div> <!-- end adviceAndRecLists -->
          </div> <!-- end newReviewsAndAdvice -->
